Recoverable examples may include transient network failures, expired UI state, interrupted requests, or retry-safe operations.

Do not automatically retry destructive or financially consequential actions without fresh authorization when required.

Do not claim that a mission succeeded simply because a recovery function returned without throwing an exception.

Do not implement unrestricted self-modifying code or autonomous installation of arbitrary fixes.

